Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-multi-select, add-element-resize, add-marquee-selection

Goal:
Allow multiple selected resizeable canvas elements to be resized together from a shared selection box instead of only supporting resize for a single selected item.

Context:
The current resize system intentionally stays single-selection-only even after multi-select and marquee selection were added. The user now wants grouped resize behavior when several shapes are selected at once.

Expected changes:

- grouped resize handles for multi-selection
- resize math that scales all selected resizeable items from a shared bounds box
- stable behavior for mixed supported item types such as shapes, images, and imported PDF pages

Acceptance criteria:

- When multiple resizeable items are selected, the canvas shows a shared resize box with usable handles.
- Dragging a shared handle resizes all supported selected items together predictably.
- Group resize does not produce zero, NaN, or infinite dimensions and does not corrupt selection state.
- Unsupported item types, if any, are handled explicitly instead of silently breaking the interaction.

Notes:

- Keep the first pass bounded to resizeable box-like items if stroke-resize semantics are still unresolved.
- Prefer geometry captured at drag start so resize does not compound errors across pointer moves.
